= Fiscal Policy

Budgets are moral documents, and the debt limit is a recurring hostage.

- @raise_taxes: Raise taxes on high earners
- @close_loopholes: Close loopholes and boost enforcement
- @grand_bargain: Seek a grand bargain
- @easy_discard

@raise_taxes
on-arrival: budget += 3; biz_relation -= 5; working_dem += 1*(1-dissent); progressive_dissent -= 3; moderate_dissent += 2; month_actions += 1

The rich pay more; the treasury breathes easier.

@close_loopholes
on-arrival: budget += 2; biz_relation -= 2; inequality -= 1; month_actions += 1

Tax enforcement raises substantial revenue.

@grand_bargain
on-arrival: budget += 3; gopmod_relation += 6; progressive_dissent += 6; labor_dissent += 4; moderate_strength += 2; month_actions += 1

A bipartisan bargain trims deficits at some political cost.
